  "body": "## Original Work and type/producer/consumer line\n\nImplements a coherent source-owned slice of [Group stranded/opaque JSON Work #188](https://github.com/561-group/561-group-services-section/issues/188) through the existing [SEAVT issue #15](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/semiotic-eavt-services-section/issues/15). The Group's historical SEN bridge 4 KiB \u2192 44 KiB complaint must not be treated as currently unsolved: `seavt-row-json-carrier/1` already has a genuine compact encoder/decoder and the original journal writer.\n\nThe specific remaining semantic opacity is the on-disk shorthand `ej/aj/vj`. This branch makes a **new, explicitly selected** `seavt-row-json-carrier/2` using descriptive `entityJson/entityTerm`, `attributeJson/attributeTerm`, `valueJson/valueTerm`, `filedAt` and `witnessTime`, while keeping V1 as the default.\n\n## Exact original source changes\n\n- Extend the original `src/seavt-carrier.mjs` writer/reader with named V2 and strict profile dispatch, retaining the original SEN `jsonImageOf`/term identity, legacy reader and compact V1 wire behavior.\n- Forward an optional `carrierProfile` through **the existing** `appendSeavtRow` and `appendSeavtRows`; no second writer/store.\n- Own a typed **JSON Schema Draft 2020-12** V2 source at `data/schemas/seavt-named-carrier.schema.json` and package its `./named-seavt-carrier-schema` export. JSON Lines and RFC3339/UTC remain the existing framing/filing format. The schema limits container shape, while the upstream original SEN type checker admits term syntax.\n- Add native regression cases in `test/named-carrier.test.mjs`: complete JSON and SEN mixed roundtrip, V1 backwards compatibility, schema and decoder denial, actual log append/replay, measured 4KiB carriage overhead.\n- Extend original specification's compatibility/rollout conditions.\n\nSource commit [`7ed422c`](https://github.com/red-cup-engineering/semiotic-eavt-services-section/commit/7ed422c4594776c7928c6578a0caefe06bf9fefa) is Git-readback verified: exactly six original owner files, branch one commit ahead/zero behind.\n\n## Independent receiving still required\n\nThe project is private, and the Group's CI policy refuses unadmitted GitHub-hosted private-minute workflows; none was added or triggered. **No full native dependency-installed test run, `npm pack`/publication, installed host reader or production log conversion is claimed.** Receive those original tests on authorized independent compute, then select an immutable released version for downstream consumers. Only then consider switching specific writers to opt-in named V2; never flip the default or migrate existing logs merely for names. Treat the Group debt entry as historical testimony until independently measured current traffic.\n\nA typed carrier is not a domain/evidentiary decision, signer, or new authored data source.",
